# Is there a way to make a circle that is exactly as big as its container? (CSS)

How can I make a circle that is exactly as big as its container?

I am trying to do this using CSS.

I have tried to use height and width but it doesn't work.

The code I have used is this:

.container {
border: 1px solid black;
}
.circle {
border-radius: 50%;
height: 100%;
width: 100%;
background-color: red;
}


The circle is not the same size as the container.

Here is a codepen that demonstrates the problem:

https://codepen.io/anon/pen/zxqZwP

## 1 Answer

You have to use object-fit: contain; to make the circle fit the container.

